1
00:00:01,240 --> 00:00:02,000
Dr. Pun.

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:05,120
I’m Monsieur.

3
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:11,600
Now that we’ve revealed our real identities,
how about we start going out?

4
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:18,000
Be careful with your mixed signals.

5
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,320
Someone else might get to him first.

6
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:22,120
Moth.

7
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:26,080
Why don’t we just get together?

8
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:13,200
What did you say?

9
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:18,760
Uh…

10
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:21,600
Just pretend you didn’t hear that.

11
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:25,480
Moth.

12
00:02:46,079 --> 00:02:46,600
Mes.

13
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,400
How have you been?

14
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:56,840
Doing well?

15
00:02:58,800 --> 00:02:59,400
I am.

16
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:01,720
It’s been a long time.

17
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:22,160
Ah, that’s Dean.

18
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,240
My friend.

19
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:31,240
Ah.

20
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:33,200
Hi.

21
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:35,160
I’m Mes, his senior.

22
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:36,400
Senior?

23
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:43,040
Let me know when you get home.

24
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:49,800
Should we head upstairs?

25
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:53,040
Sure.

26
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:40,600
Here you go.

27
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:47,560
It’s been with me for so long.
I thought you didn’t want it back.

28
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:49,360
Of course I do.

29
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:53,200
Back in uni, I had to
save up for a month to buy this.

30
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:57,960
When you had it, did you ever read it?

31
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:02,320
Not really.

32
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:06,120
I usually use different references.

33
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:17,840
So how did you get here?

34
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:19,640
Did you drive?

35
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:22,080
I took a cab.

36
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:24,160
Why?

37
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:29,080
Now that you gave it back,
you’re trying to get rid of me already?

38
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:32,080
Nonsense, Mes.

39
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:33,760
Who would ever want to get rid of you?

40
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:38,400
Make yourself at home.

41
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:42,200
You’re still the same, Moth.

42
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:48,560
How are you doing?

43
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:51,120
I see you post a lot of work pieces on IG.

44
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,000
Do you even have time to rest?

45
00:05:57,880 --> 00:05:58,920
Work’s been pretty hectic lately.

46
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:01,200
The faster I get it done, the faster I get paid.

47
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:04,960
You should make time to travel.

48
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,680
When you decide to go to New York,
let me know.

49
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:08,800
I’ll show you around.

50
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:15,080
So, you’re back this time.
Are you staying long?

51
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:18,720
Mhm, I think I’ll be here for a while.

52
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:21,200
A gallery asked me to showcase my work.

53
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:22,960
They’re also holding a charity auction.

54
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:25,080
Hey, the exhibition opens the day after tomorrow.

55
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:29,760
Moth, you should come.

56
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:31,760
I want you to come.

57
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:57,080
[WHAT ARE YOU DOING?]

58
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:33,440
[CONGRATS, MES! WE’RE SO PROUD OF YOU.]

59
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:33,400
You got here fast.

60
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:36,080
Didn’t we say 10 a.m.?

61
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:39,360
I got here at eight to queue up.

62
00:08:39,559 --> 00:08:40,720
Isn’t that a little early?

63
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:48,240
You’re only free in the morning
because you have to be at the clinic at noon.

64
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:51,800
And there aren’t many
good breakfast places around here.

65
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:56,200
Luckily, I found this place online.
The reviews are great.

66
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:58,600
They say the food is really good.

67
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:01,040
But it’s always packed, so I had to come super early.

68
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:07,720
Don’t you like it, Dr. Pun?

69
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:09,440
I do.

70
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:12,200
But it sounds like a hassle for you.

71
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:15,960
No, it’s fine.

72
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:22,680
You’re my first boyfriend,

73
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:30,560
and this is our first time going out as boyfriends,

74
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:33,920
so I wanted to impress you.

75
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:42,280
Oh, did I say “boyfriend” too many times?

76
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:43,520
I’m sorry.

77
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:48,000
You can say it as many times as you want.

78
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:52,040
We really are boyfriends.

79
00:09:57,560 --> 00:09:59,840
Thank you for trying to impress me.

80
00:10:01,680 --> 00:10:09,040
But if we can, I’d rather we come together.

81
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:15,320
So you’re okay with coming at 5 a.m.?

82
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:18,040
I’m joking.

83
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:21,120
If we have to come at five,
we might as well find a new restaurant.

84
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:24,000
Let’s order.

85
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:05,360
Moth’s calling.

86
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:07,040
Can I answer?

87
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:08,960
Of course.

88
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:09,920
Why not?

89
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:15,680
Ah.

90
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,200
You don’t have to worry about me.

91
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:21,560
You and Moth are friends.

92
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:28,680
Hello. What’s up?

93
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:30,360
(Can we meet before noon?)

94
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:31,920
(I’ll come see you.)

95
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:41,280
Can we meet another day?

96
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:43,720
I’m with...

97
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:44,680
(Mes is back.)

98
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:52,520
(BUDDY HEAL CLINIC)

99
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:05,360
He went straight to your place
after flying back from abroad?

100
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:08,720
Not really.

101
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:11,240
He’s been back for a while.

102
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:13,480
He just…

103
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:16,560
came by to get his book.

104
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:22,400
Why didn’t you
just send it with a messenger?

105
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:30,000
I thought I was over him.

106
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:38,600
But then I saw him in person,
and I was back to square one.

107
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:43,360
I didn’t know how to act.

108
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:47,040
If I were you,
I wouldn’t have met him in the first place.

109
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:03,800
Hey.

110
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:05,880
I’m dating Ten now.

111
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:08,880
Huh?

112
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:14,040
I was going to tell you today,
but you told me about Mes first.

113
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:20,000
Then I’m happy for you.

114
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:23,400
When did you decide?

115
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:25,600
Why didn’t I know about this?

116
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:28,160
Yesterday.

117
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,240
But I’ve been talking to him for a while.

118
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:36,280
And I wanted to break out of the same cycle.

119
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:45,520
As for you, do whatever you think is right.

120
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:52,240
But if you can,
I’d rather not hear about this anymore.

121
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:17,600
I’m sorry, Pun.

122
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:19,000
There’s a bit of a problem.

123
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:21,320
Sorry about what?

124
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:25,360
Hi. Can I be your plus-one today?

125
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:27,560
Be my guest.

126
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:32,120
Hey, Pun, do you know a guy named Mes?

127
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:33,800
You’ve met him?

128
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:36,240
Yeah, big time. At Moth’s place.

129
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:41,400
Mes was Moth’s senior at university,

130
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:44,360
and also…

131
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:47,200
Moth’s first love.

132
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:52,120
Mes was someone Moth looked up to.

133
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:55,520
Moth wanted to be like him.

134
00:14:57,120 --> 00:14:59,920
He wanted to stand beside him.

135
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:16,480
Why don’t you try
adding some white as a highlight?

136
00:15:29,480 --> 00:15:30,280
Thank you, Mes.

137
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:32,840
It feels like I’m always relying on you.

138
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:34,800
You’ll surpass me very soon.

139
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:39,240
One day, you might be the one helping me.

140
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:42,160
You’re exaggerating.

141
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:45,520
Me? Better than you?

142
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:50,600
Moth, don’t ever think you’re ordinary.

143
00:15:51,160 --> 00:15:52,000
You know why?

144
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:56,200
Because you paint with your feelings.

145
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:58,520
You don’t care whether it’s right or wrong.

146
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:01,240
Precision and skill can be learned.

147
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:03,720
But feelings are what truly belong to us.

148
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:08,560
If you let your feelings flow and stay true to them,

149
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:20,240
they’ll show through in your work.

150
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,200
Promise me, Moth.

151
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:27,960
Don’t ever let that disappear.

152
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:32,360
I’d love to keep seeing it.

153
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:41,480
Well, if you don’t disappear from my life,
you’ll get to keep seeing it.

154
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:44,640
Art brought those two together.

155
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:47,680
I wasn’t in the same faculty as Moth,

156
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:51,440
so I don’t know if Mes
was simply interested in his work

157
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:54,560
or if, deep down, he felt something more.

158
00:16:56,360 --> 00:17:00,520
But hearing Moth talk about Mes every day,
I knew one thing for sure.

159
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:03,560
Moth had truly fallen in love with him.

160
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:11,599
Until one day, Moth had a wake-up call.

161
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:20,440
Happy Valentine’s, Mes.

162
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:28,200
I’m not into this kind of thing.

163
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:37,600
Are you?

164
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:44,440
Well…

165
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:48,320
Not really.

166
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:56,920
You know what’s funny?

167
00:17:57,880 --> 00:18:00,640
A year later, Mes went abroad to study.

168
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:02,760
He started dating someone

169
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:06,280
and posted new content with his partner
every Valentine’s Day.

170
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:10,760
But Moth ended up hating Valentine’s Day instead.

171
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:14,560
Mes’s partner had an impressive profile,

172
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:17,400
so Moth thought he wasn’t good enough.

173
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:23,880
Could anyone really make
Moth feel like he wasn’t good enough?

174
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:31,200
Deep down, everyone compares themselves to others.

175
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:33,120
Especially Moth.

176
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:36,840
The guy who never says
what he really thinks out loud.

177
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:47,680
If Moth was that heartbroken over him,
then why is he still being nice to him?

178
00:18:50,240 --> 00:18:53,880
All this time, he’s been mean
to everyone who’s tried to hit on him,

179
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:57,600
partly because of
the hurt he still carries inside…

180
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:04,120
and partly because he still can’t get over Mes.

181
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:36,360
Hello.

182
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:38,160
(Are you free to talk?)

183
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:42,520
What’s up, Mes?

184
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:49,040
(I opened the book you gave me
and found all these notes.)

185
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:52,760
(They brought back memories, so I called.)

186
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:59,480
(I remember you were such a nerd
about contemporary and abstract art.)

187
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:10,480
But I forgot all about it now.

188
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:11,680
(Don’t lie.)

189
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:15,080
(You don’t just forget things like that.)

190
00:20:20,520 --> 00:20:25,560
(Hey, that photo of the artwork
you put in the book, I saw the original.)

191
00:20:26,040 --> 00:20:26,680
Really?

192
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:32,040
(Yes. I’m telling you, the actual piece was
stunning. It was even better than the photo.)

193
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:42,440
We’re heading somewhere next.

194
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:46,520
You want to come with us?

195
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:51,080
Only asking out of courtesy, though.

196
00:20:53,040 --> 00:20:53,480
Ten.

197
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:58,880
Yeah, I know you want some alone time with Pun.

198
00:21:00,720 --> 00:21:01,400
I won’t get in your way.

199
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:02,960
Have fun.

200
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:12,240
Hey. I forgot to say something important.

201
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:15,600
I’m really happy for you.

202
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:22,080
You deserve a love this good.

203
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:28,720
And thank you, Pun,
for opening your heart to Ten.

204
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:33,400
I believe he can make you happy.

205
00:21:34,120 --> 00:21:37,880
I want to make Ten happy, too.

206
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:46,920
We’re off now.

207
00:21:47,280 --> 00:21:48,600
Yeah. See you later.

208
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:06,440
[WHAT ARE YOU DOING?]

209
00:22:33,840 --> 00:22:35,360
(Hey, I gotta go.)

210
00:22:35,360 --> 00:22:37,320
(I’ve got some work to finish.)

211
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:49,760
[20 MISSED CALLS FROM MANIAC]

212
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:55,040
Hello.

213
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:57,760
I saw your missed calls.

214
00:22:58,560 --> 00:22:59,560
(I’m downstairs.)

215
00:22:59,840 --> 00:23:00,520
(Come down and meet me.)

216
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:05,800
Why was your line busy?

217
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:07,120
Because I was on the phone.

218
00:23:07,800 --> 00:23:08,320
Who were you talking to?

219
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:10,920
A senior.

220
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:13,640
You wouldn’t know him.

221
00:23:13,800 --> 00:23:14,640
Is he really just a senior?

222
00:23:15,440 --> 00:23:16,760
You two talked for an hour.

223
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:19,120
If you’re going to be like this,
I don’t want to talk.

224
00:23:20,160 --> 00:23:20,560
Wait.

225
00:23:24,320 --> 00:23:24,840
Fine.

226
00:23:27,120 --> 00:23:27,840
Where are you going tomorrow?

227
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:29,320
Out.

228
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:31,000
I’ve got something to do.

229
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:31,840
With who?

230
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:36,520
I need to deposit a check.

231
00:23:36,600 --> 00:23:37,200
And then?

232
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:38,160
Are you spending all day
depositing your check?

233
00:23:38,160 --> 00:23:39,000
What’s wrong with you?

234
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:40,960
Just say whatever you want to say.

235
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:41,760
Oh, can I?

236
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:47,840
Then crystallize your thoughts
and figure out what you really want to say.

237
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:50,760
Wait.

238
00:23:53,480 --> 00:23:55,360
Fine. I’ll say it.

239
00:23:56,800 --> 00:23:57,680
Let me ask you something.

240
00:24:03,840 --> 00:24:04,640
What are we, exactly?

241
00:24:13,680 --> 00:24:14,200
I don’t know either.

242
00:24:36,960 --> 00:24:37,640
Please, come in.

243
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:39,960
Sorry, my place is a little messy.

244
00:24:41,240 --> 00:24:43,080
You can sit right here.

245
00:24:49,560 --> 00:24:52,000
We have a guest today, girl.

246
00:24:52,640 --> 00:24:54,400
How are you doing, sweetheart?

247
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:57,720
Wow.

248
00:24:57,960 --> 00:24:58,800
Let’s have some snacks.

249
00:24:59,360 --> 00:25:00,800
You’ve got your yum-yum.

250
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:04,600
Would you like to hold her?

251
00:25:05,160 --> 00:25:05,800
Whoa.

252
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:07,520
She looks so much healthier.

253
00:25:29,720 --> 00:25:33,800
Dr. Pun, you can play with Mademoiselle for now.

254
00:25:34,640 --> 00:25:37,640
I need to upload and submit my work file.

255
00:25:38,520 --> 00:25:39,240
It won’t take long.

256
00:25:39,920 --> 00:25:40,480
Of course.

257
00:25:40,840 --> 00:25:41,680
Take your time.

258
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:43,480
I’ll stay here with her.

259
00:25:44,480 --> 00:25:45,160
All right, then.

260
00:25:53,760 --> 00:25:57,680
Does your papa even know
what I’m doing at his house?

261
00:26:03,320 --> 00:26:03,920
Shit!

262
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:10,000
I think the transformer outside just blew.

263
00:26:15,800 --> 00:26:16,840
The technician hasn’t come to fix it yet.

264
00:26:18,120 --> 00:26:19,120
It should take a while.

265
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:23,040
Dr. Pun, would you rather leave now?

266
00:26:23,360 --> 00:26:24,080
No, it’s okay.

267
00:26:25,440 --> 00:26:26,800
I’d rather stay and keep you company.

268
00:26:30,240 --> 00:26:30,960
Are you sure?

269
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:44,840
I’m sorry.

270
00:26:45,960 --> 00:26:47,200
Did I disappoint you?

271
00:26:49,320 --> 00:26:51,200
Why would you think that?

272
00:26:54,120 --> 00:27:01,240
Well, I’m afraid I’m making you feel like
I’m not what you expected.

273
00:27:04,760 --> 00:27:05,360
No.

274
00:27:07,440 --> 00:27:09,280
Everyone has their own strengths and weaknesses.

275
00:27:10,680 --> 00:27:13,760
To me, you’re a really good listener.

276
00:27:19,120 --> 00:27:19,760
Then…

277
00:27:22,560 --> 00:27:24,640
I’ll just listen to you talk.

278
00:27:26,800 --> 00:27:27,640
What should I talk about?

279
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:32,840
I think my life is pretty boring.

280
00:27:34,960 --> 00:27:40,680
How about telling me things
that help me get to know you better?

281
00:27:42,480 --> 00:27:43,320
Um…

282
00:27:44,520 --> 00:27:46,200
You already know my name.

283
00:27:46,840 --> 00:27:50,160
My date of birth? I was born on October 15.

284
00:27:51,360 --> 00:27:52,280
Bachelor’s degree in veterinary medicine.

285
00:27:53,240 --> 00:27:56,040
I only have one close friend. That’s Moth.

286
00:28:05,520 --> 00:28:11,600
Mes being back this time
doesn’t just affect Dean and Moth.

287
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:14,280
You’re right.

288
00:28:15,880 --> 00:28:18,600
It affects me, too.

289
00:28:20,440 --> 00:28:22,000
I have to keep consoling Dean.

290
00:28:30,880 --> 00:28:32,400
It reminds me of the past,

291
00:28:36,400 --> 00:28:37,800
when I secretly had a crush on Moth.

292
00:28:40,560 --> 00:28:41,960
Moth secretly had a crush on Mes.

293
00:28:43,840 --> 00:28:47,440
We just kept going around in circles, endlessly.

294
00:29:04,720 --> 00:29:07,000
But I never want to
go back to that same cycle again.

295
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:12,520
Because I have you now.

296
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:23,600
I really want to
open a new book and start reading.

297
00:30:05,800 --> 00:30:05,840
Thank you for tucking Mademoiselle in.

298
00:30:05,840 --> 00:30:10,200
Thank you for tucking Mademoiselle in.

299
00:30:15,880 --> 00:30:16,880
But it’s not that late yet.

300
00:30:18,640 --> 00:30:22,120
But you have to drive home. I’m worried.

301
00:30:24,040 --> 00:30:24,680
Get home safe.

302
00:30:48,960 --> 00:30:49,640
I’m sorry.

303
00:30:50,520 --> 00:30:51,960
I’ll be leaving now.

304
00:31:04,040 --> 00:31:04,600
Pun.

305
00:31:05,800 --> 00:31:06,560
You just…

306
00:31:07,560 --> 00:31:08,160
Forget it.

307
00:31:08,600 --> 00:31:09,240
No, no.

308
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:10,760
I mean…

309
00:31:12,040 --> 00:31:15,560
I didn’t think you were ready for this.

310
00:31:19,840 --> 00:31:22,560
Then why do you think
I followed you home today?

311
00:31:25,200 --> 00:31:27,280
I thought you wanted to play with my dog.

312
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:34,200
Do you think it’s too soon?

313
00:31:38,080 --> 00:31:38,480
I…

314
00:31:40,920 --> 00:31:41,160
Yes.

315
00:31:44,720 --> 00:31:47,080
But I don’t mind, though.

316
00:31:51,040 --> 00:31:52,000
I don’t either.

317
00:32:37,920 --> 00:32:38,360
Hi, Dean.

318
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:40,880
Hey! You’re not late at all.
Everyone’s leaving.

319
00:32:41,200 --> 00:32:41,960
But you’re still here, aren’t you?

320
00:32:42,040 --> 00:32:42,560
Right.

321
00:32:43,200 --> 00:32:45,200
Whoa!

322
00:32:47,760 --> 00:32:48,680
Take it easy.

323
00:33:09,160 --> 00:33:09,960
Whoo!

324
00:33:12,320 --> 00:33:13,360
What did I do wrong?

325
00:33:13,560 --> 00:33:14,800
How is he better than me?

326
00:33:14,920 --> 00:33:17,760
♪ My heart feels numb ♪

327
00:33:19,280 --> 00:33:20,680
A rocker has possessed him.

328
00:33:20,920 --> 00:33:22,680
Shit! What did I do?

329
00:33:22,880 --> 00:33:23,880
I got it bad.

330
00:34:06,840 --> 00:34:07,600
A bottle of beer.

331
00:34:55,360 --> 00:34:55,960
Hey, Moth.

332
00:34:58,480 --> 00:34:59,840
Why didn’t you call when you got here?

333
00:35:03,440 --> 00:35:04,200
So, what do you think?

334
00:35:04,560 --> 00:35:06,680
Seeing my work now,
don’t you have anything to say?

335
00:35:07,640 --> 00:35:08,440
Go ahead and slam it.

336
00:35:09,840 --> 00:35:10,440
Are you crazy?

337
00:35:12,440 --> 00:35:13,440
Why would I slam your work?

338
00:35:16,200 --> 00:35:19,680
As if I could ever paint something like this.

339
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:20,640
Of course you could.

340
00:35:21,880 --> 00:35:23,320
You absolutely could.

341
00:35:30,320 --> 00:35:32,000
Your colors are still as precise as ever.

342
00:35:33,560 --> 00:35:33,880
No.

343
00:35:34,680 --> 00:35:35,480
They’re even more precise than before.

344
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:40,720
You were good before.

345
00:35:42,600 --> 00:35:43,880
And now, you’re even better.

346
00:35:45,280 --> 00:35:49,120
I guess that’s what an artist is supposed to be.

347
00:35:49,680 --> 00:35:51,360
I just paint the way my feelings tell me to.

348
00:35:52,160 --> 00:35:53,200
Just like you.

349
00:35:56,760 --> 00:35:59,760
When I work, all I think about are deadlines.

350
00:36:00,480 --> 00:36:01,360
Will I finish on time?

351
00:36:02,280 --> 00:36:03,600
If I do it this way,
will the client ask me to change it?

352
00:36:05,720 --> 00:36:07,200
Will people like my drawing style?

353
00:36:08,400 --> 00:36:09,320
What’s trending these days?

354
00:36:10,600 --> 00:36:14,320
But in the end, it all comes down to
how you feel, doesn’t it?

355
00:36:20,040 --> 00:36:20,520
No.

356
00:36:26,240 --> 00:36:30,480
When I work, I haven’t felt
anything for a long time.

357
00:36:39,360 --> 00:36:40,400
Then that’s a shame.

358
00:36:41,720 --> 00:36:44,480
Because that’s exactly your charm.

359
00:36:51,200 --> 00:36:55,160
But I think I can still see it in you.

360
00:36:59,600 --> 00:37:00,120
What do you see?

361
00:37:01,760 --> 00:37:02,600
Please. Don’t say something ridiculous.

362
00:37:03,120 --> 00:37:04,360
Hey, Moth.

363
00:37:06,280 --> 00:37:08,120
You still think you’re ordinary, don’t you?

364
00:37:11,200 --> 00:37:12,040
But to me,

365
00:37:17,520 --> 00:37:18,600
you’re the most special person there is.

366
00:37:26,240 --> 00:37:27,640
Walk around and take a look.

367
00:37:28,520 --> 00:37:29,440
I have to do a photoshoot with the press.

368
00:37:30,600 --> 00:37:31,160
I’ll be right back.

369
00:37:33,560 --> 00:37:33,840
Sure.

370
00:37:47,520 --> 00:37:48,440
(Don’t ever think you’re ordinary.)

371
00:37:50,960 --> 00:37:51,840
(Promise me, Moth.)

372
00:37:53,160 --> 00:37:54,720
(Don’t ever let that disappear.)

373
00:37:56,880 --> 00:37:58,280
(I’d love to keep seeing it.)

374
00:38:16,400 --> 00:38:17,280
Did you follow me?

375
00:38:21,320 --> 00:38:23,040
Yeah. I did.

376
00:38:23,920 --> 00:38:27,000
I wanted to see how many times
one person can turn into a lovesick dog.

377
00:38:28,760 --> 00:38:29,360
How funny.

378
00:38:30,080 --> 00:38:31,800
You’ve spent all these years heartbroken,

379
00:38:33,160 --> 00:38:34,280
yet the moment he says
something nice to you,

380
00:38:35,160 --> 00:38:36,600
you’re grinning from ear to ear.

381
00:38:37,880 --> 00:38:38,840
Are you really that happy?

382
00:38:44,200 --> 00:38:44,680
Are you drunk?

383
00:38:46,080 --> 00:38:46,760
Drunk? No.

384
00:38:47,160 --> 00:38:49,280
If you’re not drunk, then what are you?

385
00:38:54,160 --> 00:38:54,560
Jealous?

386
00:38:58,480 --> 00:38:59,680
Jealous of what? Huh?

387
00:39:00,440 --> 00:39:01,120
Why would I be?

388
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:02,800
We’re friends.

389
00:39:05,360 --> 00:39:06,080
Am I even allowed?

390
00:39:11,640 --> 00:39:12,160
Hey.

391
00:39:14,680 --> 00:39:15,600
Is he the friend I met that day?

392
00:39:17,600 --> 00:39:18,320
I guess so.

393
00:39:19,560 --> 00:39:20,520
Just like Moth said.

394
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:22,560
I’m just a friend.

395
00:39:25,360 --> 00:39:28,080
I’m glad you came to see my exhibition.

396
00:39:34,240 --> 00:39:35,360
You graduated overseas, right?

397
00:39:36,120 --> 00:39:39,360
Should I greet you the Thai way,
or should we shake hands?

398
00:39:42,440 --> 00:39:44,160
Can I get a selfie, please?

399
00:39:44,280 --> 00:39:46,200
I’d like to brag that I know someone famous.

400
00:39:55,080 --> 00:39:55,680
Whoo!

401
00:39:58,240 --> 00:40:01,680
I just followed you.
Don’t forget to follow me back.

402
00:40:05,840 --> 00:40:08,120
Mes, I’ll take my friend home.

403
00:40:10,280 --> 00:40:10,720
Moth.

404
00:40:13,920 --> 00:40:15,280
There’s a party tonight.

405
00:40:16,160 --> 00:40:19,080
I want to introduce you to someone.

406
00:40:21,040 --> 00:40:22,760
You can bring your friend along.

407
00:40:28,080 --> 00:40:30,560
I’m not sure if I can stay until then.

408
00:40:30,760 --> 00:40:31,360
But I can.

409
00:40:33,880 --> 00:40:36,160
I’ll see you tonight, Mes.

410
00:40:36,920 --> 00:40:37,280
Come here.

411
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:49,800
Stop acting crazy and go home.

412
00:40:50,120 --> 00:40:50,880
Why do you have to yell?

413
00:40:52,400 --> 00:40:54,520
Do you even realize what you’re doing?

414
00:40:55,000 --> 00:40:55,520
I do.

415
00:40:56,720 --> 00:40:58,280
I’m getting to know your senior.

416
00:40:59,120 --> 00:41:00,000
Isn’t he famous?

417
00:41:01,160 --> 00:41:02,720
I want to know a competent artist.

418
00:41:03,800 --> 00:41:04,680
Maybe it’ll make me look smarter.

419
00:41:10,920 --> 00:41:12,480
Go sleep it off for a night or two.

420
00:41:14,080 --> 00:41:15,120
We’ll talk when you’re sober.

421
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:23,440
Okay.

422
00:41:24,480 --> 00:41:25,120
I’ll go home.

423
00:41:26,000 --> 00:41:29,160
But I’ll see you tonight anyway.

424
00:41:31,400 --> 00:41:31,800
No.

425
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:33,520
Don’t come.

426
00:41:33,640 --> 00:41:34,000
Why not?

427
00:41:34,520 --> 00:41:36,520
Didn’t you hear him? He invited me, too.

428
00:41:39,080 --> 00:41:42,560
If you f*cking come,
I’ll hate you for the rest of my life.

429
00:42:02,200 --> 00:42:03,320
Let me introduce you to Sam.

430
00:42:05,600 --> 00:42:08,520
I’ve been following his work since his uni days.

431
00:42:09,520 --> 00:42:10,440
Hi, Sam.

432
00:42:11,080 --> 00:42:12,760
Oh, hey, Mes.

433
00:42:12,840 --> 00:42:15,080
Congratulations.
The exhibition was a huge success.

434
00:42:15,400 --> 00:42:17,200
Seeing how many people showed up
made me jealous.

435
00:42:17,960 --> 00:42:18,600
Thank you.

436
00:42:19,600 --> 00:42:21,840
Sam, this is Moth.

437
00:42:22,560 --> 00:42:23,720
He was my junior in the same faculty.

438
00:42:24,920 --> 00:42:27,440
He’s making art, too.

439
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:30,440
Hello.

440
00:42:30,600 --> 00:42:31,160
Hello.

441
00:42:31,840 --> 00:42:33,200
What kind of artwork do you do?

442
00:42:33,800 --> 00:42:36,520
Drawing? Painting? Sculpture?

443
00:42:37,640 --> 00:42:38,120
Ah.

444
00:42:39,680 --> 00:42:40,800
I’m a character artist.

445
00:42:46,320 --> 00:42:48,600
I do graphic design sometimes, too.

446
00:42:51,640 --> 00:42:53,440
Oh, that’s interesting.

447
00:42:56,360 --> 00:43:00,960
I saw his work. He’s really talented.

448
00:43:02,680 --> 00:43:03,080
Hey.

449
00:43:04,040 --> 00:43:05,840
Chat and his friends are looking for you.

450
00:43:06,200 --> 00:43:07,640
They might have a great project for you.

451
00:43:07,960 --> 00:43:08,640
Why don’t we go talk to them?

452
00:43:08,880 --> 00:43:09,200
Of course.

453
00:43:12,600 --> 00:43:14,400
Moth, I’ll be right back.

454
00:43:15,680 --> 00:43:16,120
Sure.

455
00:43:21,120 --> 00:43:21,720
Mes is here.

456
00:43:22,200 --> 00:43:24,200
I heard you had a good project for him.

457
00:43:24,680 --> 00:43:25,240
Hi, Chat.

458
00:44:06,800 --> 00:44:08,360
(Go sleep it off for a night or two.)

459
00:44:10,320 --> 00:44:11,440
(We’ll talk when you’re sober.)

460
00:44:18,480 --> 00:44:19,160
Hey.

461
00:44:20,080 --> 00:44:22,880
I think you should just tell him
and get it over with.

462
00:44:26,840 --> 00:44:28,280
Tell him you like him.

463
00:44:29,200 --> 00:44:30,920
Tell him you can’t stand
the thought of him leaving.

464
00:44:40,040 --> 00:44:40,680
Excuse me for a minute.

465
00:44:42,840 --> 00:44:43,120
Moth.

466
00:44:47,040 --> 00:44:48,400
I’m going to Chat’s house party afterward.

467
00:44:49,400 --> 00:44:49,880
Come with me.

468
00:44:52,320 --> 00:44:53,040
It’s okay.

469
00:44:54,280 --> 00:44:57,560
You go ahead. I think I’ll head home.

470
00:44:59,000 --> 00:44:59,840
What’s the hurry?

471
00:45:01,880 --> 00:45:02,640
Do you have plans with someone?

472
00:45:05,200 --> 00:45:08,200
I need to finish an illustration.
I’m already two days late.

473
00:45:10,320 --> 00:45:11,240
You go to the party.

474
00:45:13,320 --> 00:45:15,440
I’ll go home and make a living.

475
00:45:20,560 --> 00:45:20,960
Moth.

476
00:45:24,160 --> 00:45:25,240
Will you paint again?

477
00:45:30,160 --> 00:45:31,240
I am painting.

478
00:45:32,280 --> 00:45:33,000
No.

479
00:45:37,040 --> 00:45:39,920
I’m not talking about those comic characters.

480
00:45:41,840 --> 00:45:42,440
I mean…

481
00:45:49,080 --> 00:45:51,520
I think you know what I mean.

482
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:10,960
Paint again, Moth.

483
00:46:14,080 --> 00:46:16,200
Give me a chance to see your work again.

484
00:46:25,560 --> 00:46:28,680
And don’t worry about whether anyone buys it.

485
00:46:30,520 --> 00:46:31,400
Because I will.

486
00:46:33,280 --> 00:46:35,320
No matter how expensive it is.

487
00:48:00,480 --> 00:48:02,800
[MANIAC]

488
00:48:10,200 --> 00:48:10,840
(Hey.)

489
00:48:13,040 --> 00:48:14,320
(I’m sorry I crossed the line.)

490
00:48:17,680 --> 00:48:19,440
I don’t know what got into me.

491
00:48:21,320 --> 00:48:22,280
I was a f*cking asshole.

492
00:48:24,800 --> 00:48:26,160
If I were you, I’d kick my ass.

493
00:48:31,640 --> 00:48:32,400
(I’m sorry.)

494
00:48:34,040 --> 00:48:34,760
(I…)

495
00:48:36,840 --> 00:48:37,840
Can you not hate me?

496
00:48:41,640 --> 00:48:42,640
(Please don’t hate me.)

497
00:49:06,040 --> 00:49:06,440
Here.

498
00:49:54,640 --> 00:49:57,240
The artist party wasn’t fun?

499
00:49:59,120 --> 00:50:00,960
Is that why you came out here
to sit by yourself?

500
00:50:01,600 --> 00:50:02,440
What’s there to have fun about?

501
00:50:04,440 --> 00:50:07,680
Those people don’t know how to have fun.

502
00:50:10,240 --> 00:50:11,240
Aren’t you one of those people?

503
00:50:17,000 --> 00:50:17,520
Good point.

504
00:50:20,040 --> 00:50:20,960
I don’t know.

505
00:50:23,480 --> 00:50:27,480
Let’s just say I know what fun is.

506
00:50:29,320 --> 00:50:32,320
And being with those people isn’t it.

507
00:50:34,400 --> 00:50:35,080
Should we hit a nightclub?

508
00:50:36,360 --> 00:50:37,400
Have some crazy fun.

509
00:50:38,080 --> 00:50:40,680
No. I’d rather stay here.

510
00:50:48,040 --> 00:50:54,800
Have you forgiven me
for what happened at the gallery?

511
00:50:58,160 --> 00:50:58,800
Don’t talk about it.

512
00:51:00,440 --> 00:51:01,080
I don’t want to dig it back up.

513
00:51:17,480 --> 00:51:18,560
I want to be a cat.

514
00:51:22,520 --> 00:51:23,040
Huh?

515
00:51:24,160 --> 00:51:24,960
I want to be a cat.

516
00:51:27,240 --> 00:51:30,280
Maybe things will get easier.

517
00:51:34,320 --> 00:51:35,120
Are you all right?

518
00:51:37,600 --> 00:51:38,080
You okay?

519
00:51:40,400 --> 00:51:45,240
Right now, I don’t know if
I’m doing something I actually like.

520
00:51:46,920 --> 00:51:51,200
I don’t even know who I am anymore.

521
00:51:58,800 --> 00:51:59,960
Is there anything I can help you with?

522
00:52:07,760 --> 00:52:08,600
Can’t think of anything now.

523
00:52:11,160 --> 00:52:12,360
You can tell me when you do.

524
00:52:16,120 --> 00:52:16,920
Um…

525
00:52:22,560 --> 00:52:23,640
Can I sleep on your lap?

526
00:52:44,080 --> 00:52:46,240
Anything else you want?

527
00:52:48,960 --> 00:52:49,720
Um…

528
00:52:54,080 --> 00:52:55,080
Will you sing for me?

529
00:52:55,960 --> 00:52:56,320
What?

530
00:52:59,760 --> 00:53:03,280
I’m afraid that’ll just stress you out more.

531
00:53:05,640 --> 00:53:06,320
Come on.

532
00:53:09,080 --> 00:53:09,920
You’re not going to do it?

533
00:53:19,600 --> 00:53:25,880
♪ Stay with me tonight
If there’s no one there to hold you ♪

534
00:53:26,080 --> 00:53:30,440
♪ Stay with me
Until the morning light breaks through ♪

535
00:53:40,920 --> 00:53:45,760
“You don’t have to stand your ground
on everything. Your legs will get sore.”

536
00:53:47,040 --> 00:53:47,800
What are you talking about?

537
00:53:48,880 --> 00:53:49,920
Don’t you want to be a cat?

538
00:53:50,640 --> 00:53:51,880
Then try thinking like one.

539
00:54:03,840 --> 00:54:07,240
“Never say never.
Unless you mean ‘never mind.’”

540
00:54:46,040 --> 00:54:48,080
There’s an exhibition next week.

541
00:54:48,960 --> 00:54:52,160
If you pull this off, you can finally
become a full-fledged artist.

542
00:54:52,480 --> 00:54:53,200
What should I do?

543
